1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,882
Parliament's committee agreed.

2
00:00:01,882 --> 00:00:04,468
The order would be
twenty-three used trains,

3
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:08,318
on one condition: keep building
up Indonesia's own train industry.

4
00:00:09,453 --> 00:00:10,629
Then it hit a rule.

5
00:00:10,629 --> 00:00:15,037
Indonesia's trade ministry only allows
used capital goods like these up to

6
00:00:15,037 --> 00:00:16,093
twenty years old.

7
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:20,606
The trains on offer were twenty-five
to twenty-eight years old.

8
00:00:20,606 --> 00:00:24,206
On average, they had been carrying
passengers in Japan since 1998.

9
00:00:25,313 --> 00:00:29,741
On November 5, the railway's chief
executive cancelled the plan.

10
00:00:29,741 --> 00:00:32,672
His words: for the public, it must be new.

11
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:36,220
You might guess Japan ran out of trains.

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:37,460
It didn't.

13
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:41,920
Japan still has trains to sell, but
they are too old for Indonesia's own

14
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:42,280
rule.
